      "id": "ch2",
      "title": "Suárez and the May Spark",
      "description": "Eugenio Suárez's power and clutch hitting from multiple contributors ignited a 17-11 May that breathed life back into the Mariners' season.",
      "startClipIndex": 2,
      "endClipIndex": 5,
      "tone": "turning_point"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch3",
      "title": "Grinding Through June",
      "description": "A 9-15 June tested Seattle's resolve, with bullpen cracks resurfacing at critical moments even as the offense showed flashes of brilliance.",
      "startClipIndex": 6,
      "endClipIndex": 7,
      "tone": "struggle"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch4",
      "title": "The Summer Surge",
      "description": "A historic July-August run of 38-15 baseball, powered by unexpected heroes like Cade Marlowe and Dominic Canzone alongside a maturing Julio Rodríguez, lifted Seattle into genuine playoff contention.",
      "startClipIndex": 8,
      "endClipIndex": 17,
      "tone": "triumph"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch5",
      "title": "September Unraveling",
      "description": "A brutal 11-17 September collapse, marked by late-game bullpen disasters and mounting losses in close games, extinguished the Mariners' playoff hopes and left a talented roster watching October from home.",
      "startClipIndex": 18,
      "endClipIndex": 21,
      "tone": "struggle"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch6",
      "title": "Too Late to Save the Season",
      "description": "Julio Rodríguez's 30th homer and J.P. Crawford's dramatic late-September double offered tantalizing glimpses of what might have been, but Seattle's window had already closed.",
